  "decision_date": "09/12/2019",
  "description": "Change of Use of Vacant Retail Unit (Use Class A1) to Dental Surgery (Use Class D1), with associated changes to the ground floor elevation to incorporate branding and signage\r\n",
  "site_name": "Street Record",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "29/11/2019",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": "Chiswick High Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "lapsed_date": "08/12/2022",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (0231-1000, 0231-1010, 0231-2000, 0231-2010, Location Plan and Planning Statement [received 07/10/2019], and Marketing Letter [received 20/11/2019]) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - Prior to first beneficial use of the development hereby approved, full details of the shopfront design (including entry point, glazing/window treatment, lighting, signage, fascia boards and other detailing) to comply with the Council's adopted Shop Front Design Guidelines SPD (2013) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved design shall be fully implemented and kept as such unless permission is secured otherwise.",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to first beneficial use of the development hereby approved, the applicant shall submit to and have approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority a Delivery and Servicing Plan.",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to first beneficial use of the development hereby approved, the applicant shall have submitted to and had approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority dedicated long-term cycle parking to accommodate at least six bicycles for exclusive use of staff of the dental practice, enclosed separately from any residential provision within the basement. The storage units must be made available for use prior to commencement of the new use and retained thereafter for use at all times without obstruction.",
    "Condition : 6 - The D1 use hereby permitted for a dental practice occupying the specified ground floor units at 231-245 Chiswick High Road shall not be carried on outside the following times: 0800 - 2000 Monday to Saturday; 0800 - 1700 Sundays and Bank Holidays.",
    "Condition : 7 - The premises shall be used for dental surgery and for no other purpose (including any other purpose in Class D1 of the Schedule to the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification)."
  ],
